The shaders in this directory are loaded at runtime by SimGear's ShaderVG
(simgear/canvas/ShaderVG/src/shaders.c) through sgShaderVGShaderOpen(), which
looks them up as Shaders/ShaderVG/<name>. They live here as separate files to
make them easy to update.

These shaders are loaded manually using raw OpenGL calls. OpenSceneGraph and
Effects are not involved at all.

Files:
  pipeline.vert / pipeline.frag   the only shader program ShaderVG uses.

color_ramp.vert / color_ramp.frag were removed: that program was compiled and
linked but never drawn with. Gradient ramps are generated on the CPU
(shUpdateColorRampTexture) and uploaded as a 1024x1 texture.
Keep SimGear and FGData in step: a SimGear that still asks for color_ramp.*
will report "Could not find ShaderVG shader" at startup.

Notes on pipeline.*:
 - GLSL 330 core. Attribute locations are explicit: pos = 0, textureUV = 1.
   layout() overrides glBindAttribLocation(); shaders.c uses
   glGetAttribLocation(), so the two agree.
 - rampSampler and patternSampler both use texture unit 1 (host-assigned).
 - Output is not clamped or premultiplied; the host's blend state defines the
   OpenVG semantics.
